[Essay]  
Standardized testing should be significantly reduced as a primary assessment tool in education. Its narrow focus undermines essential skills development, like critical thinking and creativity. The current structure forces educators to concentrate on test-related content at the expense of a comprehensive educational experience. This leads to a shallow understanding that does not promote innovative or analytical skills necessary for real-world applications. Furthermore, standardized testing exacerbates educational inequities among diverse student populations. These exams often fail to accommodate students with learning differences or those from low-income backgrounds, perpetuating cycles of disadvantage and stress. The tests' reliance on a one-size-fits-all model cannot accurately measure diverse capabilities or the true potential of students and schools. Therefore, the focus on standardized testing should be reduced. This shift will allow for a more inclusive and equitable education system that values all students' unique strengths. Adopting diversified assessment strategies can cultivate a well-rounded educational environment that prioritizes the full development of every student.

