[Essay] Standardized testing, in its current form, requires urgent reform or minimization within educational systems. While it aims to ensure accountability and comparability, its uniform nature often disregards individual learning needs, undermining the personalized educational experience students deserve. If standardized testing were reformed to focus less on uniform metrics, educational equity might thrive as students from diverse backgrounds would not be disadvantaged by a one-size-fits-all system. By prioritizing individualized learning, students who previously struggled under standardized metrics could excel, enhancing overall educational outcomes. Furthermore, if we continue down the current path without reform, the undue stress and pressure associated with high-stakes testing could persist, potentially escalating mental health challenges among students and educators. This hypothetical chain of events suggests that without change, the focus on test preparation will continue to narrow the curriculum, stifling creativity and critical thinking. Therefore, reforming standardized testing is not just a possibility but a necessity to cultivate a more inclusive and well-rounded educational environment that nurtures all types of learners.

